  "review": {
    "en": "A journey through hell, purgatory and paradise in a hundred cantos of interlocking rhyme, crowded with real people Dante knew, hated or mourned. Its architecture is exact down to the number of lines, yet what stays is the voices: lovers still bound together, a teacher met in fire, a guide who must turn back. It made a vernacular Italian fit for anything.",
    "zh": "一百歌、环环相扣的韵律，走过地狱、炼狱与天堂，沿途挤满但丁认识、憎恨或哀悼的真实人物。它的结构精确到诗行的数目，留下来的却是那些声音：仍被绑在一起的恋人、火中重逢的老师、不得不止步的引路人。它让俗语意大利语足以承载一切。"
  },
